✔ compensatory: the hour arithmetic never rounds against the worker and the consent sentence states amount and deadline (2.089458ms)
✔ compensatory: policy v3 carries the ratio, the deadline and the cap with their articles, and refuses a ratio below the legal floor (6995.451958ms)
✔ compensatory: consent is the employee's alone, explicit, recorded with its sentence, and immutable (8088.279375ms)
✔ compensatory: approval credits hours × the accepted ratio with the deadline counted from the work date, once (7199.124792ms)
✔ compensatory: leave-compensated overtime never reaches payroll as overtime pay, by either door (7311.797209ms)
✔ compensatory: leave is consumed from the oldest credit first, in half days too, and cancelling returns the hours to the same credits (6349.971083ms)
✔ compensatory: without an accepted working-time policy the type refuses and names that policy and its owner — no assumed eight hours (6121.9945ms)
✔ compensatory: an accepted version-2 policy keeps reading exactly as before — no compensatory type, no choice, nothing invented (6179.821708ms)
✔ compensatory: a credit past its deadline is raised by the daily sweep, proposed as overtime pay by a human, and nothing is ever deleted (7239.152125ms)
✔ compensatory: when the employee leaves, the unused hours block the settlement until they are proposed as overtime pay (5969.559666ms)
✔ compensatory: the yearly cap is measured when the choice is made, and what exceeds it stays payable as overtime (5373.849084ms)
✔ compensatory: overtime approved as time off before the ledger existed is credited by a human, not lost (5443.509375ms)
✔ compensatory review: an exit payout never goes to a month with no payroll line — a locked exit month names who reopens it, and the hours stay due (5336.06025ms)
✔ compensatory review: when the exit month is already approved no run can carry the pay — it is an open item on the settlement, carried by a written decision and kept with it (3136.328667ms)
✔ compensatory review: leave approved for a date after the service ended is not «used» — it blocks the settlement until it is cancelled, then its hours are paid (3588.8185ms)
✔ compensatory review: a hand-written overtime movement is refused while leave-compensated hours are unsettled — next month and before approval too — and the approver sees one that came first (3281.335875ms)
✔ compensatory review: hours past their deadline are not leave any more, even for a back-dated request — the payout queue does not shrink under the preparer (2938.028042ms)
✔ compensatory review: a working-time policy accepted between reservation and approval does not debit a day at the old length — the request goes back to be reserved again (2976.033417ms)
✔ compensatory review: split payouts of one credit never return more overtime than was worked, at a ratio that does not divide evenly (2943.049166ms)
✔ compensatory review: the company cap on overtime pay (Art. 77(5)) never blocks the pay of unused compensatory hours — the approver is told, and decides (2874.148917ms)
✔ compensatory review: the employee never sees a fake zero — «غير متاح» with its reason when no policy is accepted, and approved hours not yet credited are shown to their owner (5832.104333ms)
✔ compensatory review: the payroll pre-run check counts what is really due — a credit still inside its deadline is a notice, not «انقضت مهلته» (2891.904416ms)
✔ compensatory review: INSERT OR REPLACE cannot rewrite a recorded consent or a credit (2990.706125ms)
✔ compensatory UI: the overtime form offers the choice, shows the exact sentence the server stores, and sends consent only when ticked (6100.650417ms)
✔ compensatory UI: «الإجازات» shows the balance in hours and days with each credit's deadline and the 14-day warning; attendance shows the queues to their holders only (2933.642167ms)
